  fold at z/d 0.171: |E|^2 grows from it with exponent 2.01 across, horizontal, 1.84 across, the other normal, 4.02 along the tangent (from 0.01 to 0.02 a); 2.001, 1.989, 4.002 below 0.003 a
  fold at z/d 0.829: |E|^2 grows from it with exponent 1.98 across, horizontal, 2.13 across, the other normal, 3.97 along the tangent (from 0.01 to 0.02 a); 1.999, 2.011, 3.998 below 0.003 a
  along loop 0 the softer normal gradient runs 2.70 to 9.08 E_rms/a (3.37 times), 2.70, 2.70 at the folds; the stiffer 3.67 to 11.37
  height turns: a trefoil in two-bridge position 4, a Hopf link of round circles 4 (its linking number +1.000)
  [folds: 0.1 s]

== sections: the worked field in section, and the escape path (figure 5) ==
  the saddle at s = 0.01919, azimuth -121.4 deg: its Hessian's eigenvalues -6.20, 3.40, 18.65 (of mean |E|^2 per a^2); descending either way it reaches loop and cap, the path rising nowhere above the saddle (0.01888)
  [sections: 2.5 s]

== power: depth against power at 2.45 GHz, and the thresholds (figure 6) ==
  fields carried in from far away (RFG-2): 7.8 × 10⁻⁵ eV per watt; 25 meV takes 320 W, 1 eV 1.3 × 10⁴ W
  the worked cavity's null loops: 3.8 × 10⁻⁴ eV per watt; 25 meV takes 67 W, 1 eV 2664 W
  facing boards, h = 0.5 mm, 10 kOhm (RFG-3): 3.7 eV per watt; 25 meV takes 0.0067 W, 1 eV 0.27 W; the slope holds to 7.03 eV (q = 0.908)
  four rods, h = 0.5 mm, 10 kOhm (RFG-3): 15 eV per watt; 25 meV takes 0.0017 W, 1 eV 0.067 W; the slope holds to 17.36 eV (q = 0.908)
  the side wall's |E|^2 peaks at 0.942 of the mean: 18.4 meV per watt of ponderomotive energy, so copper's 30 to 100 eV crossover at 513 to 1711 W for returning electrons (3.17 U_p) and 203 to 678 W for crossing ones (8 U_p); air at 3 MV/m peak at 10.8 kW; 10 to 30 kV/m at the antinodes at 0.12 to 1.08 W
  [power: 0.0 s]

